WEBVTT

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.520
Look, the sky up above has begun to move.
Hora miageta sora ugokidashita yo

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.750
Your astonishment was so dazzling.
Odoroku kimi mabushikute

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.810
Should I forgive the lies you told me yesterday
Kinou tsuita uso mo yurusou kana

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.050
just because the morning light is so pretty?
Kesa no hikari kirei dakara

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:38.170
The sound of your laughter is always important to me
Kimi no warai goe itsu datte daiji da yo

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.820
because it gives me courage.
Yuuki kureru kara saa

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.680
It's not a lie.
Uso ja nai

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.460
It's a beauty really
It's a beauty really

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.610
Your voice whenever.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.110
It makes me have.
Your voice whenever.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:50.990
It makes me have.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:51.660
Even the silliest things sound dear,
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
It makes me have.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:57.980
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
Even the silliest things sound dear,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.540
if it's your voice I hear.
kimi no koe nara

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.810
You're sad whenever.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.120
It takes you back.
You're sad whenever.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:05.460
It takes you back.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:08.840
My heart runneth over.
Hamidasu kokoro

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:16.040
Unable to control myself, I set off at a run.
Osaerarenakute hashiri dashita yo

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.050
I can forever.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.550
It's a bright and sunny day today.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.120
It's as if it never rained yesterday.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.370
Don't sleep in too much
just because it's a day off.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.340
Come on, Tsukasa-chan.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.730
The weather's great.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.600
Do you want to go shopping?

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.000
I'll buy anything you want for you.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.930
I don't need anything... anything at all.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:05.930
A Present with All One's Might

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.060
Just get up already, Tsukasa-chan!

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.410
I'm fine. I just want
to be lazy right now.

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:13.840
What are you saying?

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.330
It's almost lunchtime.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.440
Oh, the phone's ringing.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.340
I'll get it!

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.060
H-Hello. This is Nishino.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:28.350
Umm, is Tsukasa-chan there?

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.320
Oh, it's you, Tomoko.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.270
What do you mean,
"It's you, Tomoko"?

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.890
Anyway, are you free today?

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.630
I wanted to get some clothes, wanna come along?

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:40.810
Today is...

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.160
Ehh, you can't?

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:45.930
I suppose I can go.
Maybe I'll buy something too.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.860
Okay, see you later.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.080
Who was that? A friend of yours?

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.260
Are you going out, Tsukasa-chan?

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.790
Yes, at 1:00.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:59.400
Hey, Mom, is it okay if I buy something for myself?

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.410
It's okay. But Tsukasa-chan, today is...

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.580
I understand, I'll be back by 6:00.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.950
Just be sure to bake
a cake by then, Mom.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:16.210
Aren't you glad you found some clothes you liked, Tomoko?

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:20.050
Yeah, but it was hard to limit myself to one pair of jeans.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.730
There's a lot more stuff I want, too.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.110
You bought a pair of good boots, right?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:26.720
Well, kind of...

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:30.520
And they were 20,000 yen!
Are you loaded or something?

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.010
It's not like that.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:35.980
When I said I was going shopping, my mom went and gave me an allowance.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.820
Today's special.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.950
Special?

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:43.190
I really want a part-time job.

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.330
But it's against school rules.

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.830
Wow, it's wonderful!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.080
It's the pendant I told you I wanted.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.810
It's a surprise gift for the first
anniversary of the day we met.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.740
It was pretty expensive, so treasure it, Aa-chan.

00:03:56.740 --> 00:03:59.770
So, you even remember things like that, Ko-chan?

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:02.310
Of course I do! What, you thought I'd forget?

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.720
Yeah, I did.

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.340
Tsukasa!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.090
Eh? W-What?

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.620
You've been watching that couple over there for a while.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.750
You don't have a boyfriend, do you?

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.850
If you're that jealous, just get one.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:17.010
These days, some boys at the high schools around here

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:19.940
have their eyes fixed on you,
and the rumors are flying.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.360
They're saying that you reject any suitors without mercy.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.380
No voice mails or texts?

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.080
Yo!

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.510
Sorry, did I keep you waiting?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:33.860
Who's <i>he?</i>

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.410
Whoa, whoa, you didn't tell her about me?

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:40.530
Didn't I mention him?

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.770
He's my senpai from middle school,

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:45.800
and he kept going on about
how he just <i>had</i> to meet you.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.940
Ehh, so that's how it is.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.230
I'm really sorry.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:52.560
But isn't this good?

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.200
He's pretty cool,

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.450
and there are a lot of girls that want to go out with him, but can't.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.400
That concludes <i>this</i> conversation; I'll leave you two alone now!

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.920
H-Hey! Wait a minute, Tomoko!

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.410
Hey, it's all good.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.180
Dammit Tomoko, you stiffed me on the juice bill.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.800
Hmm, you look pretty cute in casual clothes, too.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.450
Even so, you're pretty
strange, Tsukasa-chan.

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.400
Why aren't you going out with anyone?

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:21.380
You'd have no shortage of willing guys.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.350
Being with someone is a lot more fun than being alone.

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.240
Ow!

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:35.320
Just what were you about to do there?

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:36.490
I can't believe you!

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:39.220
But, you looked so lonely, so...

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:41.620
That's no reason to do something like that!

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.610
Why not? It's all good.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:47.840
I thought something like that would deepen our friendship.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.740
A single kiss doesn't mean
anything in this day and age.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.130
You see, a kiss is just a greeting. An introduction.

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.680
It's just like a handshake.

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:58.110
I'm leaving.

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:00.470
Why? Don't tell me you're angry?

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.600
Sorry, but it seems like our values don't match at all.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.760
Now aren't you a pure one,
Tsukasa-chan?

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:12.810
I'm home.

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.320
I was kept late...

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:16.690
How's Tsukasa?

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:17.980
Well, you see...

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:22.650
She's shut herself in her room ever since she came back from shopping.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:27.170
So, "A kiss is just a greeting"?

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:31.050
I just don't understand,
since I've never been kissed.

00:06:32.170 --> 00:06:32.740
But...

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.680
This really sucks.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:44.000
Whose ring tone was this annoying?
I don't remember setting this song.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:51.180
Hmm? Nishino isn't answering.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.260
Junpei! Did you see Yui-chan off?

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:56.700
Yeah, awhile ago!

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:57.910
Seriously...

00:06:58.320 --> 00:06:59.230
Junpei-kun?

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.060
Nishino? I'm amazed that you can recognize me without hearing my voice.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.900
Sorry for calling you on a day off.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:12.430
My childhood friend said that she wanted
to go to Oumi Academy next year.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:16.120
She asked me if I knew
anyone who got in there.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.140
I was wondering if it was okay to mention you.

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:20.790
I want to meet up.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:24.350
You want to meet her?

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.980
I want to meet <i>you.</i>

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.610
Can I see you right now?

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:34.330
Eh? But it's already 10:00,
and I just got back home.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:39.320
I want to see you today,
no matter what.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.940
Please, Junpei-kun.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:49.840
Nishino sounded like she was crying for a moment there.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.060
Did something happen to her?

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.710
What happened?

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.010
Nishino!

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:09.740
You ran to my side.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:10.670
Thank you.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.720
What? Nishino is smiling.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:17.720
But, I'm sorry for calling you out here when you were tired.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.910
N-No, I wasn't all that tired.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.940
So, Nishino, what is it?

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.080
You don't know what this is?

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:31.280
It's strawberry shortcake.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:35.090
Uhh, that's not what I meant...

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:40.060
My mom was the one who made these.

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.250
Shall we sit down and eat them?

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:44.550
Uhh... okay...

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.920
Say, um...

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.390
Umm, was this what
you wanted to do?

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.300
That's right.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.450
Oh, t-that was it.

00:09:01.360 --> 00:09:02.370
Please try it.

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.100
Sure.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.870
You see, this cake was...

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.040
...something I wanted you to eat today, no matter what.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:19.140
Because today's my birthday.

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:21.860
Eh? Really?! Seriously?!?

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:25.350
N-Never mind, erm... congratulations.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:28.000
What should I do?
I really didn't know.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.630
This is bad. I didn't get you anything,
but you can have this strawberry.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:34.650
Thank you.

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.300
But I like this.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.100
I didn't think I'd actually be able to spend time with you.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.210
I won't ever forget your birthday again, Nishino.

00:09:44.210 --> 00:09:45.410
Really, I swear.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.650
And more importantly, a present...

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:49.490
Why don't we go and
buy one tomorrow?

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.170
But we have school tomorrow.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.860
Ah, that's right.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.490
So, what do you want, anyway?

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:00.490
Can I ask for anything?

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.200
As long as it's something I can afford.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.730
What? Is there cream
stuck to my face?

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:10.670
No, it's not that...

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:14.760
Could you... give me a handshake?

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:16.770
A handshake?

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:17.730
Yeah.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.190
No, it's okay, you can tell me what you really want.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.710
Well, this is probably

00:10:26.710 --> 00:10:30.400
the thing most I want you to do,
more than anything else.

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:35.150
Erm, that is...

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:14.070
Thanks. I should be
heading home about now.

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.110
See you later, Junpei-kun.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.570
G-Good night, Nishino.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:24.550
Good night.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:40.010
I wonder if Nishino's hand feels
as warm as mine does right now.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:45.270
I... I...

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:57.870
Literature Club

00:11:57.870 --> 00:12:00.990
Sorry for making you stay with me this late, Maki-chan.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.500
I took too much time editing this tape.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.290
I wonder if Toujou is still there.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.910
Toujou Aya-sama

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.290
What's that? A love letter?

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:12.110
That's so cool.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.550
Who's it from? Who's it from?

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.630
Someone I don't know.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.530
Why don't you try meeting him?

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.950
He might be a really wonderful person.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:21.700
But, I...

00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:23.880
Ah, I get it!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.570
There's somebody you like, Aya-chan!

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:31.600
Was I right? Hey hey, who is it?
Tell me, Aya-chan!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:32.980
Are you already dating him?

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:34.850
It's an unrequited love...

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.640
I see...

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.200
It's all thanks to him...

00:12:40.950 --> 00:12:41.860
"All thanks to him"?

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:46.990
He knows that I'm writing a novel.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:50.450
Because that person encouraged
me to go after my dream.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.120
But, he has a girlfriend.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:58.630
I-I see...

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:01.590
I wonder if I have no choice but to give up.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.630
Aya-chan...

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.600
Just kidding!

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:09.050
That was just the plot for my novel!

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:12.040
That's a lie.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:14.230
That was the truth, wasn't it?

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:16.860
Like I said, it's the plot of my novel.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:19.510
Right now, I'm having too much fun writing my novel

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:20.770
to think about liking someone...

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:22.830
Is that really true?

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:31.790
A Sensation of Unknown Destination

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:34.580
Toujou has feelings for me...?

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.290
If that's really how she feels... I...

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:42.030
No, that's impossible.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:50.720
There's also Satsuki and Nishino... plus,

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:53.770
it really could be just
a novel storyline.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.210
I couldn't get any sleep...

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.980
I can't decide who's the best.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.980
But I can't let this
situation go on forever.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.620
Good morning, Manaka!

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.120
I've missed you so much over the last 12 hours, my darling!

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:21.200
D-Darling?! What's with that?

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.840
It's an expression of love,
an expression of love.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:29.130
Because our relationship is <i>serious,</i> isn't it?

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.180
A "serious" relationship?

00:14:35.690 --> 00:14:38.720
You know, your memory must be screwed up.

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.850
When did we take things to that level?

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.540
Think it over carefully.

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:44.410
Okay? We haven't really...

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.400
But didn't you embrace me?

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:54.220
I want everyone in the world to know

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.550
about the events of that hot night!

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:59.080
Quit acting stupid! Stop it, Satsuki!

00:14:59.560 --> 00:15:01.770
But, you were inexperienced, weren't you?

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:04.960
I wanted you to say that
until the very end.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:08.480
I-I don't know what
you're talking about!

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:11.800
Oh my! You don't have to get so embarrassed!

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:17.270
A-Anyway, nothing really happened that day!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:18.730
Noth-ing!

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:23.020
Hey! Manaka, where are you going?

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.810
Seriously, just what is she thinking?

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:31.910
Joking around that much...

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:35.740
Well, of course
I was a <i>little</i> happy, but...

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.460
G-Good morning...

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:42.920
Good morning.

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.420
Ah, that reminds me. Here, take this.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:48.460
Bye.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.220
Toujou--

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:58.100
After all, Manaka-kun has Nishino-san.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.560
I have to stop thinking about him.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.230
I have to stop thinking--

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:10.950
When you toss a coin,

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:13.550
whether heads or tails comes up is entirely random.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.740
Satsuki...

00:16:15.770 --> 00:16:16.500
And it is impossible to know beforehand what it will be.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:17.590
Toujou...

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.280
And it is impossible to know beforehand what it will be.

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:21.160
Nishino...

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:25.210
What am I supposed to do?

00:16:26.480 --> 00:16:31.460
So, you've come to me with your desirable "problem"?

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:33.980
I understand it's desirable, but...

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:37.140
That's why I can't talk to Komiyama about it...

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:40.310
Lend me some of your wisdom, Oukusa-sama.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:44.190
Lost between three girls, huh?

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:47.940
<i>I</i> would just go out with all of them at once.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:52.990
